  "caption": "Footy day: Quinn took a knee straight to the thigh and tried to run it off. Kay, on the sideline, had other ideas.\n\nA corked thigh is a bruised quadriceps muscle. Most settle in one to two weeks with a calm, sensible start.\n\nWhat often helps: stop playing, rest with the knee bent, use ice and compression early, then begin gentle, pain-free knee bending. Rebuild range, then strength, then sprinting before returning, and wear a thigh guard when you're back. Deep massage or hard stretching on a fresh cork isn't the shortcut it seems.\n\nGet it checked if the thigh gets harder or worse after two to three weeks, the knee still won't bend after two weeks, or it aches at night.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
